On 8/4/08, peter hering <pjhering@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>
>
> This has gone on too long.
> .i la'e di'u ranji ze'u
>
>

The rest of these were perfect as far as I could tell.  Here "ze'u" just
means for a long time, so "ranji ze'u" is just "continues for a long time",
not for "too long."  There's a very convenient and interesting word "za'o"
which is for just this purpose: "za'o ranji" means "continues beyond its
natural ending point", goes on too long.

mu'o mi'e se ckiku

